t4p4-switch
===========

The P4Pi setting. Edit /root/t4p4s-switch to contain only a single line as follows.
tunnel1

tunnel1.p4
==========
Source program for the switch BMV2 .
This to be copied in the directory /root/bmv2/examples/tunnel1
This file is same for both the P4Pis and infact same in all 
P4Pis in case of multi node implementation.

p4edge-setup
============
This file is modified version of the file
/usr/sbin/p4edge-setup
This file is same for both the P4Pis and infact same in all 
P4Pis in case of multi node implementation.

After the reboot of the P4Pi, the following scripts are to be 
execute to reach our test setup,

bmv2-start
==========
This is modified script that are executed by the bmv2.service.
During development, we modified to include logs and removed those
changes later. In crypto settings, the script is modified to include 
additional ports.

setup1_test
===========
The file contains shell commands to initialize Linux briges
and other relevant settings. These commands are specific for each P4Pi.
Modify interface name of USB-Ethernet port accordingly.
setup1_test_p4pi1 and setup1_test_p4pi2 are respective setup1_test 
scripts for p4pi1 and p4pi2 devices.

s1_test.txt
===========
The file contains data to load the Match-Action tables of the ingress 
pipeline. These are specific for the P4Pi. To be modified accordingly.
The file s1_test_p4pi1.txt is specific for P4Pi1 of our test setup.
The file s1_test_p4pi2.txt is specific for P4Pi1 of our test setup.

cp.sh
=====
A helping script to pupulate Match-Action tables in one shot. Modify as required.

csrc.sh
=======
A helping, one shot script, that  copies source files to relevant directories and 
do things as needed.

Rust installation and setup
===========================

Install Rust in P4Pi . Visit the Rust site and follow install instruction. It is a
single shot execution for installation.

cp the directories enc and dec under Rust_files. To compile the encryption binary.
Go to enc directory and compile by the following command. Similarly for decryption 
binary that is available under dec directory.
cargo build --release

The binaries are available under target/release/enc for encryption and accordingly
for the decryption. This binaries caan be directly executed.

All Rust files are common for all P4Pi devices. 
keys.txt
========
As we use symmetric key encryption, the keys are shared. The file keys.txt should 
be copied into /root directory.
